---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Bump this whenever the policy text changes; the change clause promises it.
const updated = '11 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy · John Pettitt" description="What p.tt collects about visitors: nothing. What its host logs, and how this policy changes.">
  <header class="top col">
    <a class="home" href="/">John Pettitt</a>
  </header>

  <main class="col doc">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses no cookies, no analytics, no trackers and no advertising identifiers. Every file it loads, fonts and
      images included, comes from p.tt itself. I have no server-side code here and nothing that receives information
      about you.
    </p>

    <h2>What the host sees</h2>
    <p>
      p.tt is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub's documentation says that when a GitHub Pages site is visited, "the
      visitor's IP address is logged and stored for security purposes, regardless of whether the visitor has signed
      into GitHub or not." That logging is GitHub's, under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>; I don't see or receive it.
    </p>

    <h2>The live clock</h2>
    <p>
      The world clock on the home page is <a href="https://github.com/jpettitt/geo-clock-card">geo-clock-card</a>
      running in your browser. It reads your device's clock to draw day and night, uses NASA imagery served from this
      site, and never asks for your location: the dot is Nevada City, not you. Nothing it computes leaves your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage</h2>
    <p>The site stores nothing in your browser: no cookies, no local storage, no session storage.</p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Links go to GitHub, Medium, LinkedIn, Google Patents, Home Assistant and geoclock.world. Once you follow one, that site's own
      privacy policy applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the date at the top changes and the revised version is posted at this same address. If the
      site ever starts making a request to another service, this page will say so in the same update.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions go to j@ this domain.</p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .top {
    padding-top: 56px;
  }

  .home {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .doc {
    margin-top: 48px;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .doc h1 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 6px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .doc h2 {
    margin-top: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .doc p {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
</style>
